# Cases that reproduce bugs which were REAL. Found under generator version 1.
#
# BUG-0044 — a truncated ozz archive was read into partially uninitialised
# memory and built into a Skeleton anyway. ozz's IArchive is documented as
# trusting its input ("reading cannot fail") and enforced that with DEBUG-ONLY
# asserts, so the same corrupt cooked mesh ABORTED in debug and was SILENTLY
# ACCEPTED in release, on the AsyncLoader thread.
#
# Fixed by anim::GuardedStream (records every short read, refuses the result)
# plus a patch removing ozz's read-side asserts so debug and release agree.
# Against the pre-fix tree this seed aborts on archive.h's assert.
12660276661850738527

# BUG-0046 — a corrupt COUNT field that ozz read successfully and then allocated
# from, tripping its own sanity check (animation.cc:81, timepoints <= uint16 max).
# A short-read guard structurally cannot see this: nothing comes up short. Fixed
# by mesh format v6 — an FNV-1a digest ahead of each opaque blob, so ozz is only
# ever handed bytes whose digest matched.
#
# Found under generator version 1; still reproduces under version 2, which
# digests the PRISTINE blob and then corrupts it (the cooker-writes-then-disk-
# corrupts model) rather than corrupting in place with no digest at all.
4648068295214073242
